{
 "_comment": [
  "Search results pages that search engines may index (owner 2026-10-19: the search is the site's strength - the key terms' results belong in Google).",
  "q: the query as the page's path runs it (/<q>, default scope); its results page gets index,follow, its own title and description with the number of suttas, and a sitemap entry (en, ru). Every other query stays noindex, follow.",
  "ru, en: the owner's glossary (Google Sheet \"Mapping Pali-Rus\", Лист1 columns C and D, the first rendering; the tab \"SEO-термины\" lists these terms with live lookups). A term without an entry goes without that gloss.",
  "index: false - the query catches other words (ogh -> mogha; diacritics fold, so jāti -> uppajjati, bhava -> bhavati), held back until its query is settled.",
  "A term with kinds (SN 45.161-180, owner 2026-10-20): the word at a word start plus its kinds as the canon lists them, as a regex; patterns are not diacritic-folded and run up to 128 characters. Bhava: its compounds and noun forms, not bhavaṁ (sir) or bhavati. Yoga: the four bonds only, not yogakkhema.",
  "Part 2 (owner 2026-10-20: «только им падеж самое основное»): the nominative forms only, singular and plural, as whole words. Kilesa (owner: «очень модное слово»): the nominative is 3 suttas, so every word with kiles - kilesa, upakkilesa, saṅkilesa - all of them the same defilement.",
  "slug: the page's address when q is a regex (owner 2026-11-28: a path like /\\bindriyaṁ\\b|… opened for no one and Google refused it); the old /<q> address 301s to /<slug>."
 ],
